    "created_at": "2026-01-30T09:28:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-30T09:28:42Z",
    "body": "i could see some use in having events that were fired as a result of keyboard interaction to have undefined, negative, or some other \"unique\" values, to provide authors with another way to disambiguate when something was a result of a keyboard interaction (and leaving it up to assistive technologies to find the element's center point and providing those coordinates when they \"fake\" mouse events for compatibility). using zero is perhaps ambiguous, as there is a very small chance that this was indeed the set of coordinates that were clicked by a mouse?\n\non the other hand, it's probably simpler to say that by default, if the coordinates aren't provided for the event, it defaults to the center of the bounding box of the element it's being dispatched to.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
