    "created_at": "2026-01-30T09:34:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-30T09:34:16Z",
    "body": "> i could see some use in having events that were fired as a result of keyboard interaction to have undefined, negative, or some other \"unique\" values, to provide authors with another way to disambiguate when something was a result of a keyboard interaction (and leaving it up to assistive technologies to find the element's center point and providing those coordinates when they \"fake\" mouse events for compatibility).\n\nNow that clicks are PointerEvents rather than MouseEvents, authors can use the `pointerId` or `pointerType` to detect if a non-pointing device invoked it. A keyboard sets the `pointerId` to `-1` and `pointerType` to `\"\"`.",
