    "created_at": "2026-02-02T16:06:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-02T16:12:32Z",
    "body": "> So what we'd really like to do is clarify the specification on this and require the midpoint of the target element to be used.\n\nThat feels very surprising in case the focused element is outside the viewport. See for example \nhttps://mozilla.pettay.fi/moztests/keyclick.html\n\nBlink and Gecko report 0,0, Webkit on linux at least report coordinates way outside the viewport. It is unclear to me how those outside-the-viewport coordinates could be used to position a menu in a reasonable way.\n\nI think, maybe, that since we can't really guarantee very useful coordinates, reporting 0,0 consistently and asking one to rely on event's target and pointerType might lead to better outcome.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
