    "updated_at": "2026-02-11T14:57:16Z",
    "body": "IMO, unless the UA reports a random x,y inside the target element (and also fakes the layerX/Y, clientX/Y, page, offset, etc.), it's no different than 0,0 when it comes to privacy and detecting keyboard/AT use. If privacy is the primary concern, that's what I'd suggest. Otherwise, codifying 0,0 makes sense. I can bring up the privacy concern in the next APA call.\n\nThe argument against fake coords would be for recreating a session from event data for the purposes of debugging. Fake coords will make that technique a waste of time.",
